  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "Catch it and hold on",
  "description": "Pairs with one ball, 4–5 metres apart. With an odd number of players, make one group of three. Everyone gets to be a goalkeeper here.\n\nThrow the ball to your partner at different heights: at the stomach, at the chest and just over the head. The catcher brings the ball in to the body with the arms under and around it, like a scoop, or first catches it with both hands and then pulls it in. When that works, the thrower runs in after the throw and gives the catcher a gentle shoulder bump – the ball should stay put. Swap roles after five throws.\n\nHarder: throw higher so the catcher has to jump for it, roll the ball straight at your partner, and then to the side so your partner has to get down to it. Finish by punching the throws back with the fists. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Watch the ball all the way into your hands."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Hands out towards the ball – then in to the chest."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Hug the ball with your elbows close together so it can't slip out."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Bump gently: your partner should feel it, not get hurt."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
